- 4 buckets (4 tables): Pending, cleared, flagged, relabelled
- pending is the default table containing new posts that have not been attended to at all
- cleared, posts checked and not considered hateful (ususally normal or abusive posts). Not worth reporting. Goes into the "cleared" bucket
- flagged: posts checked and is worth reporting (usually abusive or hate posts). Goes into into the flagged bucket.
- cleared and flagged buckes are mutually exclusive.
- relabelled: posts that the reviewer thinks is mislabelled by the model. Reviewer performs 2 actions: 1. corrects the label (normal/abusive/hate) 2. decides whether it should be flagged or cleared. If flagged, it goes into the flagged bucked, if cleared, it goes into the 'cleared' bucket. It is also added into the relabelled bucket. So the relabelled bucket is not mutually exclusive with 'cleared' or 'flagged' buckets. Changes must be persisted, a refresh should not affect the udpates made.
- FYI (for future implementation): data from the relabelled bucket will be used to retrain the model in a feedback loop. So we need to keep track of the model-prediction and the manual re-label, saved for future use.
